# TODO - Autonomous AI quiz publication

## Objective

Finish admitted AI image delivery, autonomous publication, correction,
progress, cancellation, and recovery through the canonical operations.

## Acceptance

**IT WORKS** when the teacher can ask an AI client for a quiz and the
registered product tools produce, publish, and verify it on Blooket without
requiring a routine editorial approval step. The flow must support admitted
question options and stable-ID media, show understandable progress/errors, and
correct supported mismatches without duplicate publication.

Actual attachment intake must work through an explicit, bounded path when media
is requested; do not assume ChatGPT attachments automatically arrive at MCP.
A genuine login/challenge/permission stop still requires the human. Show one
complete teacher-facing journey and focused checks; defer extra UX polish,
rare edge cases, and platform-only assurance to ongoing hardening.

## Implementation notes

Apply the two-field intake and normalization requirements from tasks 05-07 to
AI-assisted review. The AI supplies detected language, topics, and structured
normalized English metadata through admitted enrichment operations, preserving
the teacher's original name and description. Canonical asset paths remain
service-owned. Import, English source text, or an unsaved generated response is
not completed normalization.

Expose validated quiz list/read/create/edit, question type/seconds/media,
progress, and recovery through registered CLI commands and MCP tools. Keep local
JSON as automatic private drafts/execution state rather than requiring manual
file management or treating it as authority over fresh Blooket state.

Finish autonomous quiz publication, progress, cancellation, correction, and
recovery in the browser UI. Manual inspection remains available but is not a
pre-publication gate. Translate remaining states and actionable errors into
English and Spanish, preserving quiz and original-media language independently.

## Evidence

The browser runtime now has guarded text-only Create Set and Add Question
mechanics with exact post-submit read-back and persisted journal/budget
integration. Local drafts remain recovery/authoring state rather than a remote
Blooket draft authority.

## Blockers

Canonical external publication entrypoints and admitted media upload remain
functional work. No teacher approval is required before an otherwise admitted
publication; human intervention is reserved for genuine validation boundaries.
